WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:07.010
One of the most common questions I get asked
is, "Pat, what is really the difference between

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.350
a goal and a vision.

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:09.890
Is there really one?

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.470
Isn't it the same thing?

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.160
If it's different, what's different?"

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:17.270
So I took time and we wrote down some notes
on what is the difference between a goal and

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:18.270
a vision.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:21.220
And I'm going to get right into it because
the reality part of it is that there is a

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.410
very big difference.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.630
There's a very, very big difference between
a goal and a vision.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.100
Very big difference between a goal and a vision.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:33.980
I think the question sometimes people ought
to ask is, "Can a goal oriented person be

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:39.480
as good of a visionary -- can they really
be a great visionary -- and can a visionary

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.690
be an incredible goal setter?

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:42.840
That's what we're going to talk about today.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.489
So first, let's talk about the difference
between a goal setter and a visionary.

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:49.309
The one thing about a goal setter is this.

00:00:49.309 --> 00:00:54.980
Goal setters set a goal, and a goal typically
has a life span.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:55.980
Right?

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:00.760
So, for instance, I want to reach this goal
by this time and and I want to do this.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.280
I want to make $100,000 by this time.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.010
I want to buy a house by this time.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.440
I want to go and drive this car one day.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.400
I want to buy myself a Porsche.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.200
Where a vision and a visionary doesn't have
a life span.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.920
There is no deadline to it.

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:15.920
It keeps going.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:16.920
There's no deadline.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:22.320
So goal, short term, vision, long term.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:27.030
Lifespan [goal] no lifespan [vision] deadline
[goal], no deadline [vision] -- it continues

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.030
to go.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:30.229
That's one of the things that you've got to
keep in mind about the differences.

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:35.450
The other thing about goal vs. vision, a goal
is a checklist.

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:40.950
For instance, I have to do boom, boom, boom,
boom, boom to get this, right?

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:42.940
I have to do.

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.240
. . to reach this goal.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.439
That's what I have to do.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:47.740
A vision is a mission.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:49.920
We HAVE to do this.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:51.659
This has got to take place.

00:01:51.659 --> 00:01:53.580
We can do this better.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.150
This is by far the way it needs to get done.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:58.399
This is the right way of doing this thing.

00:01:58.399 --> 00:02:00.060
We're going to correct and adjust.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.030
We're going to make this a better platform.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.210
We're going to make it a better experience.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:07.280
But the visionary doesn't have 17 different
steps.

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.310
The goal setter says, "Okay [snap], here's
what we need to do - dot, dot, dot, dot dot."

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.349
Okay, that's goal, this is vision.

00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:14.780
Checklist [goal] mission [vision].

00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:17.879
There's a big difference between a goal and
a vision.

00:02:17.879 --> 00:02:19.159
Next one.

00:02:19.159 --> 00:02:21.519
Goal setters are great at being directional.

00:02:21.519 --> 00:02:24.040
Which is exactly what I just said with checklists,
but it's directional.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:27.790
First let's talk to that person and then let's
call this person then let's do this, okay?

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:33.250
That's what a goal oriented person will say
on the directions of what to do next.

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.730
A visionary will paint a picture is what they'll
do.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:38.010
Let me tell you what it looks like if we do
this.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:39.010
Here's what it's going to look like.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:42.000
Can you imagine if one day we have bop, bop,
bop, bop, bop.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.829
Can you imagine if we do this, this, this
part.

00:02:44.829 --> 00:02:46.639
Goal is going to say directional.

00:02:46.639 --> 00:02:48.840
If we want to do this, we've got to talk to
these other people.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:49.999
Then we go and get it done.

00:02:49.999 --> 00:02:53.340
Here's another thing.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.970
Goal is deadline, visionary can't stop talking
about it.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:03:03.639
You know if you're a goal setter more or a
visionary if you only talk about the next

00:03:03.639 --> 00:03:08.260
goal to hit and it's always what needs to
get done to hit that goal, you're more of

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:09.310
a goal-setter type.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:14.609
If you can't help yourself but constantly
paint a picture of what it will look like

00:03:14.609 --> 00:03:19.680
if we get it done -- feel, emotion, all of
that -- you're the visionary type.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.680
And that's the one part you've got to keep
in mind with the goal setter and the visionary,

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:23.680
right?

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.480
And the last one is just simple to keep in
mind, you have logic [goal setter], you have

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:26.480
dream [visionary].

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:30.010
It's pure logic, here's what we need to do,
here's what takes place with this, [goal setter]

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.439
and you have the dream [visionary] that takes
place.

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:34.810
Now, both are important.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:42.409
So this is not a message for me to say where
it's about, well, you know, the person who

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:45.040
sets goals is not as important as the visionary.

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:47.290
Absolutely ludicrous to make that statement.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.939
I want to say that I'm not making that statement.

00:03:49.939 --> 00:03:53.750
One is just as important as the other one.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.150
One is just as important as the other one.

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:59.799
This is the challenge though sometimes with
goal setters.

00:03:59.799 --> 00:04:01.299
Here's the challenge with goal setters.

00:04:01.299 --> 00:04:09.689
Those who are typically goal driven people
tend to sometimes slow down and sabotage themselves

00:04:09.689 --> 00:04:11.579
and revert back to bad habits.

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:14.430
Because they already reached the goal, so
now they're bored, right?

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.430
Because goals have deadlines.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.690
They have a short lifespan.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:20.419
The goal can be achieved and then you're kind
of like, "Well, what do I do next?"

00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:21.419
Right?

00:04:21.419 --> 00:04:22.419
What do I do next?

00:04:22.419 --> 00:04:26.360
You don't need to worry about that with Elon
Musk, because Elon Musk is not a goal-driven

00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:27.360
guy.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.360
He's a vision-driven guy.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:30.120
You don't need to worry about that with Jobs.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.720
He's a vision-driven guy.

00:04:31.720 --> 00:04:36.750
You don't need to worry about that with Bezos
or the Google guys or certain coaches that

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:41.110
just cannot stop coaching because it's not
just about a goal, it's about a vision of

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:45.590
what organization we can build and who we
can become, and why the Yankees are the greatest

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.699
organization because we're going to change
the way that people look at the game of baseball

00:04:49.699 --> 00:04:52.680
and we're going to make the world realize
that baseball is the greatest sport in the

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.680
world.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.349
A certain soccer athlete is going to be like,
the greatest sport in the world is soccer

00:04:56.349 --> 00:04:59.970
because when you grow up with kids and all
these kids growing up, the first thing you

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:02.870
do is throw them a ball and the ball is on
the ground and it touches your feet first.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:04.020
To touch your hands you've got to pick it
up.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:05.870
A ball is not meant to touch your hands.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:08.120
They're selling you the vision of the game
of soccer.

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:11.949
Where the logical guy, the goal-setter guy
is going to say, no, here's how you play the

00:05:11.949 --> 00:05:12.949
game the right way.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:15.820
You've got to position like this and you've
got to kick like this and when you kick it's

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:19.030
got to be here and when you do the header
it's got to be.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.090
. . that's the logic side.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:22.729
So the defense has got to be.

00:05:22.729 --> 00:05:23.979
. . that's the logical side, right?

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:26.099
So can one go without the other?

00:05:26.099 --> 00:05:27.099
Absolutely not.

00:05:27.099 --> 00:05:31.710
So here's the thing about goal vs. vision.

00:05:31.710 --> 00:05:36.189
The goal setters need a visionary to team
up with.

00:05:36.189 --> 00:05:39.410
The visionaries need to surround themselves
with goal setters.

00:05:39.410 --> 00:05:43.470
Because if one doesn't do the other, that
won't become a reality.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.810
One will not become a reality without the
other.

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:50.469
There's somebody that casts a vision, there's
another one that says, "Here's how we do it."

00:05:50.469 --> 00:05:53.199
The person who is, "here's how we do it,"
will get bored.

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:56.750
This is why it's very critical for them to
always team up with a visionary.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:03.370
A lot of times visionaries try so hard to
become goal setting type of people.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:04.440
So hard.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:09.490
And they'll never even come this close to
great goal setters.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:14.680
And goal setters try so hard to become visionaries
and they fail every single time.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:15.680
Why?

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:19.650
Because they can talk like a visionary for
one day, they can cast a vision for two days,

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:22.560
three, four, five, six, seven, ten days later,
all they're talking about is what?

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:23.569
Logic and the next goal.

00:06:23.569 --> 00:06:24.569
Makes sense?

00:06:24.569 --> 00:06:26.439
They forget that their real thing is the vision.

00:06:26.439 --> 00:06:28.750
You don't need to tell the visionary to talk
about the vision.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:31.520
What you need to tell the visionary is, "here's
the next goal.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:33.080
What do we do next?

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.080
What do we have to do next?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.300
What is the next goal?"

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:38.980
That's what the visionary needs to be talked
to about . In order to have the vision become

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.059
a reality, what are the next.

00:06:40.059 --> 00:06:41.479
. . what do we need to do in the next six
months.

00:06:41.479 --> 00:06:43.210
Next month, 12 months, 24 months.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.879
That's what they need.

00:06:44.879 --> 00:06:46.629
So even though -- I want you to know this.

00:06:46.629 --> 00:06:49.870
This is not -- sometimes people will say,
"Well that's why I'm the vision guy.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.050
I don't deal with minutia."

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.050
Nonsense.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:53.050
You're making excuses.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.990
You're justifying why you don't want to improve
in an area of goal setting.

00:06:55.990 --> 00:07:00.120
I am probably not the most organized person
you'll ever meet.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.819
If you look at my desk right now, it's messy.

00:07:01.819 --> 00:07:04.949
I'm not the most organized person you'll ever
meet.

00:07:04.949 --> 00:07:08.419
In my mind, it's very clear on what vision
- I already see the movie.

00:07:08.419 --> 00:07:09.830
I've already seen the movie.

00:07:09.830 --> 00:07:13.029
I've seen the movie over and over and over
again and I've explained the movie to tens

00:07:13.029 --> 00:07:14.400
of thousands of people over and over.

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:15.729
To me, it's clear.

00:07:15.729 --> 00:07:17.090
I've already seen it.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.470
I've already seen exactly, I've felt it.

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:23.050
I've felt how people reacted when they see
the vision becoming a reality.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.960
I've seen the impact it makes around the world.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:26.830
In my mind, I've seen it.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:27.830
I've seen it.

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:31.819
That's why I need a lot of help, to help this
vision become a reality.

00:07:31.819 --> 00:07:35.449
But I can still become a better goal setter.

00:07:35.449 --> 00:07:38.389
I can still improve in my goal setting abilities.

00:07:38.389 --> 00:07:41.770
I can still sit down and grab a paper and
pen and say, "What is the next goal?

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:44.800
What are the next things that we need to do
to get to this vision?

00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:51.720
Just like a goal-setting person can create
a reminder in their phone or all around them

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:56.090
-- maybe a vision board -- to always talk
about the vision.

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:58.849
To have somebody that reminds them about the
vision.

00:07:58.849 --> 00:08:01.529
To have somebody that tells them where we're
going long term.

00:08:01.529 --> 00:08:04.569
To have somebody that doesn't just focus on
the short-term.

00:08:04.569 --> 00:08:06.740
Both people can improve.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:11.360
But no matter how much you improve -- if you're
a goal-setting type, you will never be a natural

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:13.849
visionary -- as good of a natural visionary.

00:08:13.849 --> 00:08:18.999
If you're a natural visionary type of person,
you will never be as organized as a goal-setting

00:08:18.999 --> 00:08:21.599
person that's directional, that knows what
needs to get done.

00:08:21.599 --> 00:08:25.639
Next, regardless, find them, team up together,
and the world is yours, based on how hard

00:08:25.639 --> 00:08:29.499
you work and how long you guys can work together
as a team.

00:08:29.499 --> 00:08:34.240
So, the question, the difference between a
goal setter and a visionary, that's my thoughts.

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:37.289
If you've got any questions about it, comment
